<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cdot\prod^{l-1}_{i=0}{\mathbb{P}}(S_{i+1}=\phi(r_{i+1})\mid U_{i+1}=\pi(v_{i+1}),U_{i}=\pi(v_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cdot\prod^{l-1}_{i=0}{\mathbb{P}}(S_{i+1}=\phi(r_{i+1})\mid U_{i+1}=\pi(v_{i+1}),U_{i}=\pi(v_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.9.1" class="ltx_text">Given that the graph isomorphism preserves the number of neighbors for each node and is a bijection, we can easily verify using the definitions from (<a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ B.1 Uniform random walk ‣ Appendix B Methodology - details ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) that the following indeed hold:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}(V_{i+2}=v_{i+2}\mid V_{i+1}=v_{i+1},V_{i}=v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}(V_{i+2}=v_{i+2}\mid V_{i+1}=v_{i+1},V_{i}=v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(U_{i+2}=\pi(v_{i+2})\mid U_{i+1}=\pi(v_{i+1}),U_{i}=\pi(v_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(U_{i+2}=\pi(v_{i+2})\mid U_{i+1}=\pi(v_{i+1}),U_{i}=\pi(v_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}(R_{j+1}=r_{j+1}\mid V_{j+1}=v_{j+1},V_{j}=v_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}(R_{j+1}=r_{j+1}\mid V_{j+1}=v_{j+1},V_{j}=v_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(S_{j+1}=\phi(r_{j+1})\mid U_{j+1}=\pi(v_{j+1}),U_{j}=\pi(v_{j}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(S_{j+1}=\phi(r_{j+1})\mid U_{j+1}=\pi(v_{j+1}),U_{j}=\pi(v_{j}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.10.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A3.SS2.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1,\dots,l-2\},j\in\{1,\dots,l-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1,\dots,l-2\},j\in\{1,\dots,l-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, by the assumption that the first step <math id="A3.SS2.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}\xrightarrow{R_{1}}V_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">R</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub></mover><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}\xrightarrow{R_{1}}V_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}((V_{0},R_{1},V_{1})=(v_{0},r_{1},v_{1}))={\mathbb{P}}((U_{0},S_{1},U_{1})=(\pi(v_{0}),\phi(r_{1}),\pi(v_{1})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}((V_{0},R_{1},V_{1})=(v_{0},r_{1},v_{1}))={\mathbb{P}}((U_{0},S_{1},U_{1})=(\pi(v_{0}),\phi(r_{1}),\pi(v_{1})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.11.1" class="ltx_text">But by the laws of conditional probability:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex64X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}((V_{0},R_{1},V_{1})=(v_{0},r_{1},v_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}((V_{0},R_{1},V_{1})=(v_{0},r_{1},v_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(R_{1}=r_{1}\mid V_{0}=v_{0},V_{1}=v_{1})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(V_{0}=v_{0},V_{1}=v_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(R_{1}=r_{1}\mid V_{0}=v_{0},V_{1}=v_{1})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(V_{0}=v_{0},V_{1}=v_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex64Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(R_{1}=r_{1}\mid V_{0}=v_{0},V_{1}=v_{1})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(V_{1}=v_{0}\mid V_{0}=v_{0})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(V_{0}=v_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(R_{1}=r_{1}\mid V_{0}=v_{0},V_{1}=v_{1})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(V_{1}=v_{0}\mid V_{0}=v_{0})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(V_{0}=v_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.12.1" class="ltx_text">and analogously:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex65X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}((U_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}((U_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{1},U_{1})=(\pi(v_{0}),\phi(r_{1}),\pi(v_{1})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{1},U_{1})=(\pi(v_{0}),\phi(r_{1}),\pi(v_{1})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex65Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(S_{1}=\phi(r_{1})\mid U_{0}=\pi(v_{0}),U_{1}=\pi(v_{1}))\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(U_{1}=\pi(v_{0})\mid U_{0}=\pi(v_{0}))\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(U_{0}=\pi(v_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(S_{1}=\phi(r_{1})\mid U_{0}=\pi(v_{0}),U_{1}=\pi(v_{1}))\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(U_{1}=\pi(v_{0})\mid U_{0}=\pi(v_{0}))\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(U_{0}=\pi(v_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.13.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these equalities into (<a href="#A3.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) and multiplying both sides by the equalities from (<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) for all choices of <math id="A3.SS2.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1,\dots,l-2\},j\in\{1,\dots,l-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1,\dots,l-2\},j\in\{1,\dots,l-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get precisely the equality of the right sides of equations (<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>). Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}(\eta(G,l)=\bar{\eta})={\mathbb{P}}(\eta(H,l)=\mu(\bar{\eta}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}(\eta(G,l)=\bar{\eta})={\mathbb{P}}(\eta(H,l)=\mu(\bar{\eta}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.14.1" class="ltx_text">and we can conclude that <math id="A3.SS2.p16.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\eta(G,l))\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{{\mbox{$d$}}}}}}{{=}}\eta(H,l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-2.1pt" width="0pt"><mi>d</mi></mpadded></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\eta(G,l))\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{{\mbox{$d$}}}}}}{{=}}\eta(H,l)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the algorithm <math id="A3.SS2.p16.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant in probability.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmglobalcounter8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary C.8</span></span><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmglobalcounter8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmglobalcounter8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The random walk algorithm presented in <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Uniform random walk ‣ Appendix B Methodology - details ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> is invariant in probability.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.9</span></span><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The recording protocol <math id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, as described in <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Recording function ‣ Appendix B Methodology - details ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, is invariant, provided that the embedding functions <math id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmglobalcounter9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are invariant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E,R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=(V^{\prime},E^{\prime},R^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=(V^{\prime},E^{\prime},R^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> be isomorphic knowledge graphs with the isomorphism <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=(\pi,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=(\pi,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> taking <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=(h_{q},r_{q},?)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>?</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=(h_{q},r_{q},?)</annotation></semantics></math> be a link prediction query over <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(q)=(\pi(h_{q}),\phi(r_{q}),?)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>?</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(q)=(\pi(h_{q}),\phi(r_{q}),?)</annotation></semantics></math> be its identification in <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\eta}=v_{0}\xrightarrow{r_{1}}v_{1}\xrightarrow{r_{2}}\dots\xrightarrow{r_{l}}v_{l}\in\mathcal{W}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub></mover><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">l</mi></msub></mover><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}=v_{0}\xrightarrow{r_{1}}v_{1}\xrightarrow{r_{2}}\dots\xrightarrow{r_{l}}v_{l}\in\mathcal{W}(G)</annotation></semantics></math> be a walk over <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A3.SS2.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\eta}^{\prime}=\mu(\bar{\eta})=\pi(v_{0})\xrightarrow{\phi(r_{1})}\pi(v_{1})\xrightarrow{\phi(r_{2})}\dots\xrightarrow{\phi(r_{l})}\pi(v_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mover><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">l</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mover><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}^{\prime}=\mu(\bar{\eta})=\pi(v_{0})\xrightarrow{\phi(r_{1})}\pi(v_{1})\xrightarrow{\phi(r_{2})}\dots\xrightarrow{\phi(r_{l})}\pi(v_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> be the analogous walk over <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. To prove that the recording protocol <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> outlined in <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Recording function ‣ Appendix B Methodology - details ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> is invariant, it suffices to show that the encoding of each step:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=\left(\operatorname{id}_{V}(v_{i};\bar{\eta}),\operatorname{id}_{R}(r_{i};\bar{\eta}),\operatorname{dir}_{i},\delta_{v_{i}=h_{q}},\delta_{r_{i}=r_{q}},\mathbf{v}(v_{i}),\mathbf{r}(r_{i})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>dir</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=\left(\operatorname{id}_{V}(v_{i};\bar{\eta}),\operatorname{id}_{R}(r_{i};\bar{\eta}),\operatorname{dir}_{i},\delta_{v_{i}=h_{q}},\delta_{r_{i}=r_{q}},\mathbf{v}(v_{i}),\mathbf{r}(r_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">is identical for <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\eta}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will show this for each component:</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> defines a bijection between nodes in <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{id}_{V}(v_{i};\bar{\eta})=\argmin_{t}[v_{t}=v_{i}]=\argmin_{t}[\pi(v_{t})=\pi(v_{i})]=\operatorname{id}_{V}(\pi(v_{i});\bar{\eta}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{id}_{V}(v_{i};\bar{\eta})=\argmin_{t}[v_{t}=v_{i}]=\argmin_{t}[\pi(v_{t})=\pi(v_{i})]=\operatorname{id}_{V}(\pi(v_{i});\bar{\eta}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">similarly to the point above, <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a bijection between relations of <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, so we can write:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{id}_{R}(r_{i};\bar{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{id}_{R}(r_{i};\bar{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{t}\left[r_{t}=r_{i}\lor r_{t}=r_{i}^{-1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∨</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{t}\left[r_{t}=r_{i}\lor r_{t}=r_{i}^{-1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex69Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{t}\left[\phi(r_{t})=\phi(r_{i})\lor\phi(r_{t})=\phi(r_{i})^{-1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∨</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{t}\left[\phi(r_{t})=\phi(r_{i})\lor\phi(r_{t})=\phi(r_{i})^{-1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex69Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{id}_{R}(\phi(r_{i});\bar{\eta}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>id</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{id}_{R}(\phi(r_{i});\bar{\eta}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dir}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>dir</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dir}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is clearly preserved, as the isomorphism <math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the directions of edges,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">as <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\phi</annotation></semantics></math> are bijections the masks <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{v_{i}=h_{q}},\delta_{r_{i}=r_{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{v_{i}=h_{q}},\delta_{r_{i}=r_{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, representing whether the <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’th node and relation match the types in the query, satisfy:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex70X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{i}=h_{q}\iff\pi(v_{i})=\pi(h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{i}=h_{q}\iff\pi(v_{i})=\pi(h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies\quad\delta_{v_{i}=h_{q}}=\delta_{\pi(v_{i})=\pi(h_{q})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies\quad\delta_{v_{i}=h_{q}}=\delta_{\pi(v_{i})=\pi(h_{q})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{i}=r_{q}\iff\phi(r_{i})=\phi(r_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{i}=r_{q}\iff\phi(r_{i})=\phi(r_{q})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies\quad\delta_{r_{i}=r_{q}}=\delta_{\phi(r_{i})=\phi(r_{q})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies\quad\delta_{r_{i}=r_{q}}=\delta_{\phi(r_{i})=\phi(r_{q})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I3.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I3.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are invariant by assumption, so:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}(v_{i})=\mathbf{v}(\pi(v_{i}))\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathbf{r}(r_{i})=\mathbf{r}(\phi(r_{i}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(v_{i})=\mathbf{v}(\pi(v_{i}))\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathbf{r}(r_{i})=\mathbf{r}(\phi(r_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS2.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining all these observations, we can conclude that <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\bar{\eta};G,q,\mathbf{v},\mathbf{r})=w(\mu(\bar{\eta});H,\mu(q),\mathbf{v},\mathbf{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\bar{\eta};G,q,\mathbf{v},\mathbf{r})=w(\mu(\bar{\eta});H,\mu(q),\mathbf{v},\mathbf{r})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p17.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed invariant.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmglobalcounter10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.10</span></span><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmglobalcounter10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmglobalcounter10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmglobalcounter10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The consensus protocol <math id="A3.Thmglobalcounter10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, as described in <a href="#A2.SS4" title="B.4 Consensus protocol ‣ Appendix B Methodology - details ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, is invariant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E,R)</annotation></semantics></math> be a knowledge graph and <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be isomorphic to <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> via an isomorphism <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=(\pi,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=(\pi,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{\eta}_{1:N}\in\mathcal{W}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}_{1:N}\in\mathcal{W}(G)</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of walks in <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.
To show that the output of the consensus protocol is invariant, we need to prove that for each <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{v}(v)=\mathbf{v}^{\prime}(\pi(v))\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Delta\mathbf{r}(r)=\Delta\mathbf{r}^{\prime}(\phi(r))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{v}(v)=\mathbf{v}^{\prime}(\pi(v))\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Delta\mathbf{r}(r)=\Delta\mathbf{r}^{\prime}(\phi(r))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\Delta\mathbf{v},\Delta\mathbf{r})=c(\mathbf{h},\bar{\eta}_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta\mathbf{v},\Delta\mathbf{r})=c(\mathbf{h},\bar{\eta}_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\Delta\mathbf{v}^{\prime},\Delta\mathbf{r}^{\prime})=c(\mathbf{h},\mu(\bar{\eta}_{1:N}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta\mathbf{v}^{\prime},\Delta\mathbf{r}^{\prime})=c(\mathbf{h},\mu(\bar{\eta}_{1:N}))</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}=(\mathbf{s}^{(V)},\mathbf{s}^{(R)},\mathbf{a}^{(V)},\mathbf{a}^{(R)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}=(\mathbf{s}^{(V)},\mathbf{s}^{(R)},\mathbf{a}^{(V)},\mathbf{a}^{(R)})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows from the fact that <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> are bijections – whenever <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> vertex visited in the walk <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\eta}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> node of <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\bar{\eta}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\bar{\eta}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> must be <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(v)</annotation></semantics></math> (and vice versa).
An analogous result holds for the relations.
Hence, the aggregation performed by <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>) over <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{\eta}_{1:N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\eta}_{1:N}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the aggregation for <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(v)</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(r)</annotation></semantics></math>) over <math id="A3.SS2.p19.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(\bar{\eta}_{1:N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\bar{\eta}_{1:N})</annotation></semantics></math>, and (<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is indeed satisfied.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thminnercustomprop3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_innercustomprop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thminnercustomprop3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition </span><a href="#S4.Thmglobalcounter3" title="Proposition 4.3. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical properties of Flock ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></span><span id="Thminnercustomprop3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thminnercustomprop3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thminnercustomprop3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thminnercustomprop3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flock<span id="Thminnercustomprop3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with components as described in <a href="#S4" title="4 Methodology ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is invariant in probability.</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows naturally from aggregating the results of Corollary <a href="#A3.Thmglobalcounter8" title="Corollary C.8. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a> and Lemmas <a href="#A3.Thmglobalcounter9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a> and <a href="#A3.Thmglobalcounter10" title="Lemma C.10. ‣ C.2 Invariance ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.10</span></a>, followed by applying Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmglobalcounter2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical properties of Flock ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Computational Complexity</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the iterations in each forward pass of <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Flock</span>; <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the base walk count; <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is the walk length; <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of linear sequence-model layers (such as GRU); and <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the hidden dimension for the sequence processor. Note that in practice, we perform <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> forward passes and ensemble their outputs to reduce variance. For a single pass (<math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>), walk sampling and recording cost <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the sequence processor with <math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers of hidden dimension <math id="A4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> costs <math id="A4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\ell Ld^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\ell Ld^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. The consensus protocol costs <math id="A4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\ell d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\ell d)</annotation></semantics></math>. In total, the time complexity is <math id="A4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\big(PIn\ell Ld^{2}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\big(PIn\ell Ld^{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, which scales linearly with the number of (base) walks <math id="A4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the length of walks <math id="A4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, and the number of ensembled predictions <math id="A4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. We empirically verified this in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Scalability analysis ‣ Flock: A Knowledge Graph Foundation Model via Learning on Random Walks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Compared with message-passing KGFMs like <span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Ultra</span> and <span id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Trix</span>, <span id="A4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Flock</span>’s complexity is <em id="A4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent</em> of the graph size and average degree; empirically, however, using more walks (increasing <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>) and longer walks (increasing <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>) improves coverage and yields more fine-grained representation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The space complexity of <span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Flock</span> per forward pass is <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\ell d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\ell d)</annotation></semantics></math> plus model parameters <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(Ld^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(Ld^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that running ensembles sequentially keeps peak memory near this bound, while parallel ensembling increases it by a factor of <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Scalability analysis</h2>

