<figure id="A7.T21" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 21: </span>Detailed finetuning and inference hyperparameters for <span id="A7.T21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Flock</span> in entity prediction. For each dataset, we report the finetuning epochs, batches per epoch, batch size, and the inference settings for both zero-shot and finetuned modes: test-time ensemble size <math id="A7.T21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, base walk count <math id="A7.T21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
For Hetionet finetuning we used <math id="A7.T21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,n)=(1,1024)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,n)=(1,1024)</annotation></semantics></math>, instead of <math id="A7.T21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,512)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2,512</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,512)</annotation></semantics></math> as in zero-shot.
</figcaption>
